{%- comment -%}
  K&A Welcome Offer (KLP3000) — sitewide, engagement-triggered invitation
  card. Docs/welcome-offer-popup-build-spec.md.
  Prototype: Prototypes/welcome-offer-popup-v1.html.

  RENDERED FROM: layout/theme.liquid, once, sitewide, excluding the cart
  template (see the {%- unless template == 'cart' -%} guard at the call
  site) — NOT nested inside sections/ka-nav.liquid like the search
  overlay (snippets/ka-search-overlay.liquid), because there's no parent
  section to borrow `section.settings` from when rendering directly out
  of a layout file. Instead this follows the OTHER established pattern
  for a global, singleton, theme-editor-configurable overlay already in
  this codebase — snippets/ka-concierge-float.liquid — reading copy/
  config from global `settings.*` (config/settings_schema.json, "Welcome
  Offer (KLP3000)" group) rather than a per-instance section schema.
  This still satisfies the build spec's "Suraj can edit copy from the
  theme editor without a code change" requirement exactly as well as a
  section schema would.

  ELIGIBILITY GATE (spec Section 2, condition 1) — server-side, before
  any client-side trigger logic gets a chance to run: a signed-in
  customer with at least one prior order NEVER receives this markup at
  all, not even hidden markup the JS could theoretically open. Also
  gated on the discount code setting being non-blank, so a merchant who
  clears the code field gets a clean "card doesn't exist" rather than a
  broken empty card (mirrors ka-voice-of-bride.liquid's own "don't ever
  publish placeholder/empty content" guard).

  Conditions 2-5 (no prior claim, no recent dismissal, once per session,
  not on cart / not while another overlay is open) are all client-side,
  in assets/ka-welcome-offer.js — see that file's header for the full
  state machine. The cart-template exclusion happens at the call site
  in layout/theme.liquid (this snippet never even renders there), so
  it's a third, redundant-on-purpose layer alongside the JS's own belt-
  and-suspenders check against document.body's template class.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Explicit step-by-step assigns rather than a single compound `and`/`or`
  condition — Liquid has no parentheses for grouping boolean logic, so
  `A and B or A and C` is genuinely ambiguous/error-prone to reason
  about correctly in one line. Same defensive style already used for
  ka-voice-of-bride.liquid's own has_synced_data / has_editor_content
  gate.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_returning_customer = false
  if customer and customer.orders_count > 0
    assign is_returning_customer = true
  endif

  assign should_render = false
  if settings.welcome_offer_code != blank and is_returning_customer == false
    assign should_render = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if should_render -%}
{{ 'ka-welcome-offer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="ka-welcome-scrim" id="kaWelcomeScrim" role="presentation" data-ka-welcome-redirect="{{ settings.welcome_offer_redirect | default: '/collections/all' }}">
  <div class="ka-welcome" id="kaWelcome" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="kaWelcomeTitle">
    <div class="ka-welcome__handle" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__close" id="kaWelcomeClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>

    <div class="ka-welcome__mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <span class="eyebrow ka-welcome__eyebrow">{{ settings.welcome_offer_eyebrow | default: 'A Welcome, From Us' }}</span>
    {%- comment -%}
      No inline Liquid-level `| default:` fallback here (unlike the other
      text fields below) — a literal embedded newline inside a filter
      argument string is untested/risky Liquid syntax to rely on. The
      schema default (config/settings_schema.json) already guarantees
      settings.welcome_offer_title is never actually blank once the
      theme loads on Shopify, so newline_to_br always has a real value
      to work with regardless.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <h2 class="ka-welcome__title" id="kaWelcomeTitle">{{ settings.welcome_offer_title | newline_to_br }}</h2>
    <p class="ka-welcome__body">{{ settings.welcome_offer_body | default: "Every piece we create begins with a conversation — a fitting, a fabric chosen, a silhouette considered. As you begin yours, please accept ₹3,000 toward your first, with our compliments." }}</p>

    <div class="ka-welcome__code">
      <div class="ka-welcome__code-text">
        <span class="ka-welcome__code-label">{{ settings.welcome_offer_code_label | default: 'Your Code' }}</span>
        <span class="ka-welcome__code-value" id="kaWelcomeCodeValue">{{ settings.welcome_offer_code }}</span>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__copy" id="kaWelcomeCopy" data-copy-label="{{ settings.welcome_offer_copy_label | default: 'Copy' }}" data-copied-label="{{ settings.welcome_offer_copied_label | default: 'Copied' }}">{{ settings.welcome_offer_copy_label | default: 'Copy' }}</button>
      </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Native Shopify discount deep-link (build spec §5, Flag F1) — applies
      the code to the visitor's checkout session and redirects, zero app
      dependency. Real anchor href (not JS-only) so it works even if the
      claim-tracking JS below fails to attach for any reason; the click
      handler in ka-welcome-offer.js only adds the localStorage "claimed"
      write on top of this, it doesn't replace the navigation itself.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="/discount/{{ settings.welcome_offer_code }}?redirect={{ settings.welcome_offer_redirect | default: '/collections/all' }}" class="ka-welcome__cta" id="kaWelcomeCta">{{ settings.welcome_offer_cta_label | default: 'Begin Shopping' }}</a>
    <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__email-toggle" id="kaWelcomeEmailToggle">{{ settings.welcome_offer_email_toggle | default: 'Prefer it by email? →' }}</button>

    {%- comment -%}
      Same {% form 'customer' %} pattern as sections/ka-footer.liquid's
      Inner Circle signup (build spec §5) — same contact[email] field
      name, same underlying Shopify customer-subscribe endpoint, third
      tag "welcome-offer-KLP3000" added alongside the footer's existing
      two so this acquisition source is attributable without a second,
      disconnected capture flow (Flag F4: no new Shopify config needed).

      UNLIKE the footer's version, this form is intercepted client-side
      (assets/ka-welcome-offer.js, preventDefault + fetch) rather than
      left as a plain full-page-reload submit. Reasoning: a real
      full-page navigation would tear down this popup's own open JS
      state entirely, contradicting the prototype's demonstrated
      in-place "Sent." confirmation with the card still open (Prototypes/
      welcome-offer-popup-v1.html). The <form>'s real action/method are
      left intact as a no-JS fallback (progressive enhancement, same
      principle already used for the search form in
      snippets/ka-search-overlay.liquid) — if JS fails to attach, this
      still works as a normal full-page subscribe, just without the
      inline success message. If `form.posted_successfully?` is true here
      (a real no-JS submission genuinely completed and reloaded this
      page), skip straight to the success paragraph server-side too —
      belt-and-suspenders with the JS path, not a replacement for it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- form 'customer', id: 'kaWelcomeEmailForm', class: 'ka-welcome__email-form is-hidden' -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter,ka-correspondence,welcome-offer-{{ settings.welcome_offer_code }}" />
      <div class="ka-welcome__email-row">
        <input type="email" name="contact[email]" id="kaWelcomeEmailInput" placeholder="Your email address" required />
        <button type="submit">Send</button>
      </div>
      <p class="ka-welcome__email-note">{{ settings.welcome_offer_email_note | default: "We'll also add you to The Inner Circle — collection previews and styling notes, delivered quietly. Unsubscribe anytime." }}</p>
    {%- endform -%}
    <p class="ka-welcome__email-success{% if form.posted_successfully? %} is-shown{% endif %}" id="kaWelcomeEmailSuccess">{{ settings.welcome_offer_email_success | default: 'Sent. And welcome to The Inner Circle.' }}</p>

    <p class="ka-welcome__fine">{{ settings.welcome_offer_fine_print | default: 'Valid toward your first order. One use per customer. Not combinable with other offers.' }}</p>
    <button type="button" class="ka-welcome__dismiss" id="kaWelcomeDismiss">{{ settings.welcome_offer_dismiss_label | default: 'Not today' }}</button>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
